[[eco-solving]]
=== Environment solving

**STUB**: Specifies the contract between the compiler and the environment
solver: which events trigger solving (build, install, sync), what the compiler
asks for, and what it receives back. Defines how foreign packages for each
language are provided to an environment, how the solved result is locked, and
the guarantees the lock gives (reproducibility, and when a lock is reused or
invalidated). Describes where environments and locks live and how concurrent
operations on one environment are kept safe.

